          "path": "_m/g/c/k/z/llaneilian-wp/balog-farm-llaneilian-geograph.jpg",
          "filename": "Balog Farm, Llaneilian - geograph.org.uk - 1407975.jpg",
          "caption": "Balog Farm, Llaneilian Balog is the Welsh for codpiece. But this is not the origin of the name of this farm, rather it stems from Old Irish word 'Balock' - a bishop's staff. A portrait of Eilian at Llaneilian church portrays him as a bishop. Legend states that he was Bishop of Lindisfarne.",
          "alt": "Balog Farm, Llaneilian Balog is the Welsh for codpiece. But this is not the origin of the name of this farm, rather it stems from Old Irish word 'Balock' - a bishop's staff. A portrait of Eilian at Llaneilian church portrays him as a bishop. Legend states that he was Bishop of Lindisfarne.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 408,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Eric Jones",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Balog_Farm,_Llaneilian_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1407975.jpg",
